WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.909
Naṣb. When does a word end in fatha?

2
00:00:03.359 --> 00:00:06.910
Some words in a verb sentence
answer a question about the action.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.770
What? Why? When? Where? How?

4
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.608
Those words take naṣb.

5
00:00:11.058 --> 00:00:12.633
Chapter one. Where we are.

6
00:00:12.883 --> 00:00:16.610
There are four cases. We know
two. Today we add the third.

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.678
Case A is rafʿ, with
damma. We have learned it.

8
00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:23.398
Case B is naṣb, with fatha. This
is the new one we add today.

9
00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:27.135
Case C is jarr, with kasra.
We have learned this one too.

10
00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:28.529
Case D is called

11
00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:29.615
‫جَزْم‬

12
00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:33.302
Its sign is sukūn. It is
for verbs. It comes later.

13
00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:36.180
Only past verbs. For example, he wrote.

14
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.171
‫كَتَبَ‬

15
00:00:37.421 --> 00:00:39.657
And order verbs. For example, write!

16
00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:40.739
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

17
00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:42.500
Present verbs come later.

18
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.247
And only one sign of naṣb: the
fatha, alone or with tanween.

19
00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:50.802
The other signs, for the dual and some
plurals, come later in the course.

20
00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:52.651
Each group gets its own lesson.

21
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.743
Chapter two. A new
sentence: the verb sentence.

22
00:00:57.993 --> 00:01:02.509
Last lesson, the sentence started
with a noun. Topic, then information.

23
00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:05.244
Now it starts with a
verb. Verb, then doer.

24
00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:09.153
First, the verb. A past verb
and an order verb are fixed.

25
00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:10.409
‫مَبْنِيّ‬

26
00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:13.909
Their ending never changes.
A past verb ends in fatha.

27
00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:14.900
‫كَتَبَ‬

28
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.945
An order verb ends in sukūn.

29
00:01:17.195 --> 00:01:18.027
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

30
00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:21.371
Then the doer. The doer is
the one who did the action.

31
00:01:21.521 --> 00:01:23.735
It takes rafʿ, with damma, like the topic.

32
00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:27.713
With an order verb, the doer is
you. It is hidden inside the verb.

33
00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:29.653
Example A. Zayd wrote.

34
00:01:29.903 --> 00:01:31.294
‫كَتَبَ زَيْدٌ‬

35
00:01:31.744 --> 00:01:35.585
First, the verb. Wrote. It is
a past verb, so it is fixed.

36
00:01:35.735 --> 00:01:37.346
Its fatha never changes.

37
00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:38.271
Who wrote?

38
00:01:38.621 --> 00:01:39.356
‫زَيْدٌ‬

39
00:01:39.506 --> 00:01:42.700
Zayd. That is the doer, so
it takes rafʿ, with damma.

40
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.497
Listen to the ending once more.

41
00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:46.038
‫كَتَبَ زَيْدٌ‬

42
00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:48.018
Example B. Write!

43
00:01:48.268 --> 00:01:49.100
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

44
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.306
This is an order verb.
It is fixed on sukūn.

45
00:01:52.456 --> 00:01:53.406
Who should write?

46
00:01:53.756 --> 00:01:54.585
‫(أَنْتَ)‬

47
00:01:54.735 --> 00:01:57.072
You. The doer is hidden inside the verb.

48
00:01:57.422 --> 00:01:59.712
Careful. Look at the fatha on this verb.

49
00:01:59.962 --> 00:02:00.703
‫كَتَبَ‬

50
00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.641
That fatha is not naṣb.

51
00:02:02.791 --> 00:02:05.315
A past verb ends in
fatha in every sentence.

52
00:02:05.415 --> 00:02:06.338
It is fixed.

53
00:02:06.488 --> 00:02:07.833
Naṣb is for nouns.

54
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:12.588
Chapter three. The sign of naṣb: fatha.

55
00:02:12.838 --> 00:02:17.999
It works just like damma and kasra. With
al, or when owned, it takes one vowel.

56
00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:19.828
Otherwise, it takes tanween.

57
00:02:20.178 --> 00:02:25.647
First card. With al, or when the word is
owned, it takes one fatha only. No tanween.

58
00:02:25.897 --> 00:02:27.326
With al, like the lesson.

59
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:28.431
‫الدَّرْسَ‬

60
00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.568
Or owned, like the teacher's book.

61
00:02:30.718 --> 00:02:32.704
‫كِتَابَ المُدَرِّسِ‬

62
00:02:32.954 --> 00:02:35.009
Book is owned, so it takes one fatha.

63
00:02:35.359 --> 00:02:39.868
Second card. No al. Fatha with
tanween, written with an extra alif.

64
00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:41.003
‫كِتَابًا‬

65
00:02:41.353 --> 00:02:42.433
‫صَبَاحًا‬

66
00:02:42.783 --> 00:02:44.388
Third card. The exception.

67
00:02:44.538 --> 00:02:47.749
Some words end in a round
ta, or in alif and hamza.

68
00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:51.715
They still take fatha with tanween.
But there is no extra alif.

69
00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:52.853
‫رَغْبَةً‬

70
00:02:53.203 --> 00:02:54.071
‫مَسَاءً‬

71
00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.745
Chapter four. Colour key: the new jobs.

72
00:02:58.995 --> 00:03:01.742
A big box is the word's
job in the sentence.

73
00:03:01.742 --> 00:03:04.239
A small box is a word with its own rule.

74
00:03:04.589 --> 00:03:08.699
Navy is the verb. The action.
Past and order verbs are fixed.

75
00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.126
Orange is the doer. Who did the
action? It takes rafʿ, with damma.

76
00:03:13.376 --> 00:03:15.261
The four new jobs all take naṣb.

77
00:03:15.511 --> 00:03:19.506
Pink is the object. What? Whom?
The thing the action falls on.

78
00:03:19.656 --> 00:03:23.146
Teal is the purpose. Why?
The reason for the action.

79
00:03:23.296 --> 00:03:27.203
Brown is time or place. When?
Where? With no preposition.

80
00:03:27.353 --> 00:03:30.923
Olive is the state. How? The
state of the doer or object.

81
00:03:31.173 --> 00:03:36.606
The small boxes from last lesson still
work. After a preposition. Ownership.

82
00:03:36.606 --> 00:03:38.322
Adjective. And after wa.

83
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:43.123
Chapter five. The four
naṣb jobs at a glance.

84
00:03:43.373 --> 00:03:47.684
Find the verb and the doer. For
every other noun, ask the question.

85
00:03:47.684 --> 00:03:49.614
The one it answers is its job.

86
00:03:49.964 --> 00:03:55.426
Object. What? Whom? The thing the action
falls on. The student wrote the lesson.

87
00:03:55.676 --> 00:03:58.141
‫كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ الدَّرْسَ‬

88
00:03:58.591 --> 00:04:02.782
Purpose. Why? The reason. Usually
an action noun with tanween.

89
00:04:02.782 --> 00:04:05.216
The student stood up out of respect.

90
00:04:05.466 --> 00:04:08.305
‫وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا‬

91
00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:14.100
Time or place. When? Where? No
preposition. Zayd travelled in the morning.

92
00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.465
‫سَافَرَ زَيْدٌ صَبَاحًا‬

93
00:04:16.915 --> 00:04:22.017
State. How? The state of the doer or
object, with no al. Zayd came hurrying.

94
00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.263
‫جَاءَ زَيْدٌ مُسْرِعًا‬

95
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.290
Chapter six. The object.

96
00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.169
‫مَفْعُولٌ بِهِ‬

97
00:04:30.619 --> 00:04:34.221
Here is the rule. The object is
the thing the action falls on.

98
00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:36.991
To find it, ask what,
or whom, after the verb.

99
00:04:37.141 --> 00:04:39.785
The object takes naṣb. Its sign is fatha.

100
00:04:40.135 --> 00:04:42.704
Example one. The student wrote the lesson.

101
00:04:42.954 --> 00:04:45.419
‫كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ الدَّرْسَ‬

102
00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:49.710
First, the verb. Wrote. It is
a past verb, so it is fixed.

103
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.635
Who wrote?

104
00:04:50.985 --> 00:04:52.332
‫الطَّالِبُ‬

105
00:04:52.482 --> 00:04:55.523
The student. That is the
doer, so it takes damma.

106
00:04:55.673 --> 00:04:56.643
What did he write?

107
00:04:57.093 --> 00:04:58.048
‫الدَّرْسَ‬

108
00:04:58.198 --> 00:05:01.343
The lesson. That is the
object, so it ends in fatha.

109
00:05:01.593 --> 00:05:03.140
Listen to the ending once more.

110
00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.755
‫كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ الدَّرْسَ‬

111
00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:08.401
Example two. Zayd read a book.

112
00:05:08.651 --> 00:05:10.837
‫قَرَأَ زَيْدٌ كِتَابًا‬

113
00:05:11.287 --> 00:05:15.153
The verb is fixed, and Zayd is
the doer, with damma and tanween.

114
00:05:15.303 --> 00:05:16.277
What did he read?

115
00:05:16.727 --> 00:05:17.612
‫كِتَابًا‬

116
00:05:17.762 --> 00:05:19.528
A book. It is the object.

117
00:05:19.678 --> 00:05:23.519
It has no al. So it takes fatha
with tanween, and an extra alif.

118
00:05:23.869 --> 00:05:25.861
Example three. Open the door!

119
00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:27.794
‫اِفْتَحِ البَابَ‬

120
00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.464
This is an order verb. It is fixed.

121
00:05:30.614 --> 00:05:31.466
‫اِفْتَحِ‬

122
00:05:31.616 --> 00:05:36.567
Hear the kasra on its end. It is only a
bridge to al. It is not a case ending.

123
00:05:36.817 --> 00:05:38.520
The doer is hidden. It is you.

124
00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.376
Open what?

125
00:05:39.826 --> 00:05:40.712
‫البَابَ‬

126
00:05:40.862 --> 00:05:43.887
The door. That is the
object, so it ends in fatha.

127
00:05:44.237 --> 00:05:47.086
Example four. The student
read the teacher's book.

128
00:05:47.336 --> 00:05:51.285
‫قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ كِتَابَ المُدَرِّسِ‬

129
00:05:51.735 --> 00:05:54.080
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

130
00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.204
What did he read?

131
00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:56.502
‫كِتَابَ‬

132
00:05:56.652 --> 00:05:58.809
It is the object, so it ends in fatha.

133
00:05:58.959 --> 00:06:01.242
But it is owned. So it has no tanween.

134
00:06:01.492 --> 00:06:02.928
‫المُدَرِّسِ‬

135
00:06:03.078 --> 00:06:07.285
Book of the teacher. The teacher is
the owner. The owner takes kasra.

136
00:06:07.635 --> 00:06:12.166
A tip. An order verb that ends in
sukūn takes a small kasra before al.

137
00:06:12.416 --> 00:06:14.099
‫اِفْتَحِ البَابَ‬

138
00:06:14.349 --> 00:06:15.918
‫اِشْرَبِ المَاءَ‬

139
00:06:16.168 --> 00:06:17.694
The verb is still fixed.

140
00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:21.382
Chapter seven. Purpose.

141
00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:23.858
‫مَفْعُولٌ لِأَجْلِهِ‬

142
00:06:24.308 --> 00:06:26.488
The purpose gives the
reason for the action.

143
00:06:26.588 --> 00:06:27.945
To find it, ask why.

144
00:06:28.095 --> 00:06:32.609
It is usually an action noun with
tanween, like respect, desire, or seeking.

145
00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.929
Purpose takes naṣb, so it ends in fatha.

146
00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:38.647
Example five. The student
stood up out of respect.

147
00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:41.736
‫وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا‬

148
00:06:42.186 --> 00:06:46.477
First, the verb. Stood up. It
is a past verb, so it is fixed.

149
00:06:46.627 --> 00:06:47.518
Who stood up?

150
00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.215
‫الطَّالِبُ‬

151
00:06:49.365 --> 00:06:52.406
The student. That is the
doer, so it takes damma.

152
00:06:52.556 --> 00:06:53.559
Why did he stand?

153
00:06:54.009 --> 00:06:55.090
‫احْتِرَامًا‬

154
00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.193
Out of respect. That is the purpose,
so it takes fatha with tanween.

155
00:06:59.443 --> 00:07:00.990
Listen to the ending once more.

156
00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.979
‫وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا‬

157
00:07:04.529 --> 00:07:08.211
Example six. Zayd studied
out of desire for success.

158
00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:12.055
‫دَرَسَ زَيْدٌ رَغْبَةً فِي النَّجَاحِ‬

159
00:07:12.405 --> 00:07:14.750
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

160
00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:15.869
Why did he study?

161
00:07:16.319 --> 00:07:17.207
‫رَغْبَةً‬

162
00:07:17.357 --> 00:07:20.436
Out of desire. The purpose,
so fatha with tanween.

163
00:07:20.536 --> 00:07:23.238
It ends in a round ta, so
there is no extra alif.

164
00:07:23.488 --> 00:07:24.820
‫النَّجَاحِ‬

165
00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.894
Success. The small word
before it means in.

166
00:07:27.894 --> 00:07:31.769
So success comes after a
preposition, and it takes kasra.

167
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:35.189
Example seven. Ali
travelled seeking knowledge.

168
00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:39.001
‫سَافَرَ عَلِيٌّ طَلَبًا لِلْعِلْمِ‬

169
00:07:39.351 --> 00:07:42.283
The verb is fixed. Ali
is the doer, with damma.

170
00:07:42.383 --> 00:07:43.493
Why did he travel?

171
00:07:43.943 --> 00:07:44.645
‫طَلَبًا‬

172
00:07:44.795 --> 00:07:47.685
Seeking. The purpose,
so fatha with tanween.

173
00:07:47.935 --> 00:07:49.325
‫لِلْعِلْمِ‬

174
00:07:49.475 --> 00:07:54.419
This word has two parts. The first part
means for. It is a small preposition.

175
00:07:54.669 --> 00:07:55.623
‫العِلْمِ‬

176
00:07:55.773 --> 00:07:59.350
Knowledge. It comes after a
preposition, so it takes kasra.

177
00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.726
A tip. Object or purpose?
Ask the question.

178
00:08:02.976 --> 00:08:05.162
‫قَرَأَ زَيْدٌ كِتَابًا‬

179
00:08:05.412 --> 00:08:06.386
What did he read?

180
00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:08.639
A book. That is the object.

181
00:08:08.889 --> 00:08:11.153
‫وَقَفَ زَيْدٌ احْتِرَامًا‬

182
00:08:11.403 --> 00:08:12.406
Why did he stand?

183
00:08:12.756 --> 00:08:14.794
Out of respect. That is the purpose.

184
00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:18.831
Chapter eight. Time or place.

185
00:08:19.081 --> 00:08:20.809
‫مَفْعُولٌ فِيهِ‬

186
00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:24.678
A time or place word tells us
when or where the action happened.

187
00:08:24.778 --> 00:08:26.220
It has no preposition.

188
00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.509
Ask when, or where.

189
00:08:27.659 --> 00:08:30.399
Time or place takes naṣb,
so it ends in fatha.

190
00:08:30.749 --> 00:08:33.436
Example eight. Zayd
travelled in the morning.

191
00:08:33.686 --> 00:08:35.801
‫سَافَرَ زَيْدٌ صَبَاحًا‬

192
00:08:36.251 --> 00:08:40.649
First, the verb. Travelled. It
is a past verb, so it is fixed.

193
00:08:40.799 --> 00:08:41.672
Who travelled?

194
00:08:42.022 --> 00:08:42.757
‫زَيْدٌ‬

195
00:08:42.907 --> 00:08:45.505
Zayd. That is the doer, so it takes damma.

196
00:08:45.655 --> 00:08:46.762
When did he travel?

197
00:08:47.212 --> 00:08:48.292
‫صَبَاحًا‬

198
00:08:48.442 --> 00:08:52.079
In the morning. That is time,
so it takes fatha with tanween.

199
00:08:52.329 --> 00:08:53.876
Listen to the ending once more.

200
00:08:54.026 --> 00:08:56.141
‫سَافَرَ زَيْدٌ صَبَاحًا‬

201
00:08:56.691 --> 00:08:59.394
Example nine. The boy
came back in the evening.

202
00:08:59.644 --> 00:09:01.780
‫رَجَعَ الوَلَدُ مَسَاءً‬

203
00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.475
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

204
00:09:04.575 --> 00:09:05.804
When did he come back?

205
00:09:06.154 --> 00:09:07.022
‫مَسَاءً‬

206
00:09:07.172 --> 00:09:09.915
In the evening. Time,
so fatha with tanween.

207
00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:12.675
It ends in alif and
hamza, so no extra alif.

208
00:09:13.025 --> 00:09:16.242
Example ten. The student
sat in front of the teacher.

209
00:09:16.492 --> 00:09:19.792
‫جَلَسَ الطَّالِبُ أَمَامَ المُدَرِّسِ‬

210
00:09:20.142 --> 00:09:22.487
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

211
00:09:22.587 --> 00:09:23.533
Where did he sit?

212
00:09:23.883 --> 00:09:24.804
‫أَمَامَ‬

213
00:09:24.954 --> 00:09:28.499
In front of. Place, so fatha.
It is owned, so no tanween.

214
00:09:28.749 --> 00:09:30.185
‫المُدَرِّسِ‬

215
00:09:30.335 --> 00:09:33.885
In front of the teacher. The
teacher is the owner, so kasra.

216
00:09:34.235 --> 00:09:36.604
Example eleven. Sit under the tree!

217
00:09:36.854 --> 00:09:39.301
‫اِجْلِسْ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ‬

218
00:09:39.651 --> 00:09:43.566
An order verb, so it is fixed.
The doer is hidden. It is you.

219
00:09:43.666 --> 00:09:44.490
Sit where?

220
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:45.596
‫تَحْتَ‬

221
00:09:45.746 --> 00:09:48.512
Under. Place, so fatha, and it is owned.

222
00:09:48.762 --> 00:09:49.974
‫الشَّجَرَةِ‬

223
00:09:50.124 --> 00:09:51.496
The owner takes kasra.

224
00:09:51.846 --> 00:09:54.494
Example twelve. Ali went out on Friday.

225
00:09:54.744 --> 00:09:57.914
‫خَرَجَ عَلِيٌّ يَوْمَ الجُمُعَةِ‬

226
00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:00.609
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

227
00:10:00.709 --> 00:10:01.740
When did he go out?

228
00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:02.909
‫يَوْمَ‬

229
00:10:03.059 --> 00:10:06.605
On the day of Friday. Time,
so fatha, and it is owned.

230
00:10:06.855 --> 00:10:08.003
‫الجُمُعَةِ‬

231
00:10:08.153 --> 00:10:09.525
The owner takes kasra.

232
00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:12.222
A tip. No preposition means naṣb.

233
00:10:12.472 --> 00:10:15.419
‫جَلَسَ زَيْدٌ أَمَامَ البَيْتِ‬

234
00:10:15.669 --> 00:10:16.973
No preposition here.

235
00:10:17.123 --> 00:10:18.044
‫أَمَامَ‬

236
00:10:18.194 --> 00:10:19.434
So it takes fatha.

237
00:10:19.684 --> 00:10:22.192
‫جَلَسَ زَيْدٌ فِي البَيْتِ‬

238
00:10:22.442 --> 00:10:25.912
Now the house comes after a
preposition, so it takes kasra.

239
00:10:28.266 --> 00:10:29.679
Chapter nine. The state.

240
00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:30.654
‫حَال‬

241
00:10:31.104 --> 00:10:35.023
The state tells us how the doer, or
the object, was during the action.

242
00:10:35.123 --> 00:10:36.351
To find it, ask how.

243
00:10:36.601 --> 00:10:39.320
It has no al, so it almost
always takes tanween.

244
00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.690
The state takes naṣb, so it ends in fatha.

245
00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.415
Example thirteen. Zayd came hurrying.

246
00:10:44.665 --> 00:10:46.661
‫جَاءَ زَيْدٌ مُسْرِعًا‬

247
00:10:47.111 --> 00:10:50.959
First, the verb. Came. It is
a past verb, so it is fixed.

248
00:10:51.109 --> 00:10:51.987
Who came?

249
00:10:52.237 --> 00:10:52.972
‫زَيْدٌ‬

250
00:10:53.122 --> 00:10:55.530
Zayd. The doer, so damma with tanween.

251
00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.721
How did he come?

252
00:10:57.171 --> 00:10:58.173
‫مُسْرِعًا‬

253
00:10:58.323 --> 00:11:01.412
Hurrying. That is the state,
so fatha with tanween.

254
00:11:01.662 --> 00:11:03.209
Listen to the ending once more.

255
00:11:03.359 --> 00:11:05.355
‫جَاءَ زَيْدٌ مُسْرِعًا‬

256
00:11:06.005 --> 00:11:08.663
Example fourteen. The boy came back happy.

257
00:11:08.913 --> 00:11:10.983
‫رَجَعَ الوَلَدُ فَرِحًا‬

258
00:11:11.333 --> 00:11:13.678
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

259
00:11:13.828 --> 00:11:15.035
How did he come back?

260
00:11:15.485 --> 00:11:16.402
‫فَرِحًا‬

261
00:11:16.552 --> 00:11:19.171
Happy. A state, so fatha with tanween.

262
00:11:19.521 --> 00:11:23.144
Example fifteen. The student
entered the class smiling.

263
00:11:23.394 --> 00:11:26.755
‫دَخَلَ الطَّالِبُ الصَّفَّ مُبْتَسِمًا‬

264
00:11:27.105 --> 00:11:29.450
The verb is fixed, and
the doer takes damma.

265
00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:30.461
Entered what?

266
00:11:30.811 --> 00:11:32.037
‫الصَّفَّ‬

267
00:11:32.187 --> 00:11:34.211
The class. The object, so fatha.

268
00:11:34.361 --> 00:11:35.397
How did he enter?

269
00:11:35.847 --> 00:11:36.976
‫مُبْتَسِمًا‬

270
00:11:37.126 --> 00:11:39.894
Smiling. The state, so fatha with tanween.

271
00:11:40.244 --> 00:11:42.516
Example sixteen. Drink the water cold!

272
00:11:42.766 --> 00:11:44.766
‫اِشْرَبِ المَاءَ بَارِدًا‬

273
00:11:45.116 --> 00:11:49.031
An order verb, so it is fixed.
The doer is hidden. It is you.

274
00:11:49.181 --> 00:11:49.905
Drink what?

275
00:11:50.255 --> 00:11:51.159
‫المَاءَ‬

276
00:11:51.309 --> 00:11:53.326
The water. The object, so fatha.

277
00:11:53.476 --> 00:11:54.795
How should the water be?

278
00:11:55.245 --> 00:11:56.184
‫بَارِدًا‬

279
00:11:56.334 --> 00:11:59.457
Cold. Here the state describes
the object, the water.

280
00:11:59.457 --> 00:12:01.283
So it takes fatha with tanween.

281
00:12:01.733 --> 00:12:03.625
A tip. State or adjective?

282
00:12:03.975 --> 00:12:06.623
‫جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ المُسْرِعُ‬

283
00:12:06.873 --> 00:12:11.187
The hurrying student came. The last
word has al, so it is an adjective.

284
00:12:11.187 --> 00:12:13.313
It copies the damma of the student.

285
00:12:13.663 --> 00:12:16.180
‫جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ مُسْرِعًا‬

286
00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:21.047
The student came hurrying. Now the
last word has no al, so it is a state.

287
00:12:21.047 --> 00:12:21.932
It takes naṣb.

288
00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:26.555
Chapter ten. Old rules, new ending.

289
00:12:26.805 --> 00:12:31.378
An adjective and a word after wa
still copy. Now they can copy a fatha.

290
00:12:31.728 --> 00:12:34.400
Example seventeen. Zayd read a new book.

291
00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.329
‫قَرَأَ زَيْدٌ كِتَابًا جَدِيدًا‬

292
00:12:37.679 --> 00:12:41.533
The verb is fixed. Zayd is the
doer, with damma and tanween.

293
00:12:41.683 --> 00:12:42.657
What did he read?

294
00:12:43.007 --> 00:12:43.892
‫كِتَابًا‬

295
00:12:44.042 --> 00:12:46.653
A book. The object, so fatha with tanween.

296
00:12:46.903 --> 00:12:47.841
‫جَدِيدًا‬

297
00:12:47.991 --> 00:12:51.944
New. It describes the book, so
it copies. Fatha with tanween.

298
00:12:52.194 --> 00:12:53.969
Listen to both endings once more.

299
00:12:54.119 --> 00:12:56.798
‫قَرَأَ زَيْدٌ كِتَابًا جَدِيدًا‬

300
00:12:57.348 --> 00:13:01.181
Example eighteen. The student
wrote the lesson and the homework.

301
00:13:01.431 --> 00:13:05.093
‫كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ الدَّرْسَ وَالوَاجِبَ‬

302
00:13:05.443 --> 00:13:07.967
The verb is fixed. The doer takes damma.

303
00:13:08.117 --> 00:13:09.087
What did he write?

304
00:13:09.437 --> 00:13:10.392
‫الدَّرْسَ‬

305
00:13:10.542 --> 00:13:12.701
The lesson. The object, so fatha.

306
00:13:12.951 --> 00:13:14.238
‫وَالوَاجِبَ‬

307
00:13:14.388 --> 00:13:18.644
And the homework. It comes after
wa, so it copies the lesson. Fatha.

308
00:13:20.799 --> 00:13:22.502
Chapter eleven. All together.

309
00:13:22.852 --> 00:13:26.362
Example nineteen. The teacher
opened the door in the morning.

310
00:13:26.612 --> 00:13:29.796
‫فَتَحَ المُدَرِّسُ البَابَ صَبَاحًا‬

311
00:13:30.146 --> 00:13:31.384
The verb is fixed.

312
00:13:31.534 --> 00:13:32.299
Who opened?

313
00:13:32.649 --> 00:13:33.950
‫المُدَرِّسُ‬

314
00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.030
The teacher. The doer, so damma.

315
00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.033
Opened what?

316
00:13:37.383 --> 00:13:38.269
‫البَابَ‬

317
00:13:38.419 --> 00:13:40.440
The door. The object, so fatha.

318
00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.692
When did he open it?

319
00:13:42.042 --> 00:13:43.122
‫صَبَاحًا‬

320
00:13:43.272 --> 00:13:45.918
In the morning. Time,
so fatha with tanween.

321
00:13:46.168 --> 00:13:47.875
Listen to the endings once more.

322
00:13:48.025 --> 00:13:51.209
‫فَتَحَ المُدَرِّسُ البَابَ صَبَاحًا‬

323
00:13:51.759 --> 00:13:55.348
Example twenty. Ali travelled
at night seeking knowledge.

324
00:13:55.598 --> 00:14:00.023
‫سَافَرَ عَلِيٌّ لَيْلًا طَلَبًا لِلْعِلْمِ‬

325
00:14:00.373 --> 00:14:03.893
The verb is fixed. Ali is the
doer, with damma and tanween.

326
00:14:04.043 --> 00:14:05.150
When did he travel?

327
00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.321
‫لَيْلًا‬

328
00:14:06.471 --> 00:14:08.676
At night. Time, so fatha with tanween.

329
00:14:08.826 --> 00:14:09.936
Why did he travel?

330
00:14:10.286 --> 00:14:10.988
‫طَلَبًا‬

331
00:14:11.138 --> 00:14:13.772
Seeking. Purpose, so fatha with tanween.

332
00:14:14.022 --> 00:14:15.412
‫لِلْعِلْمِ‬

333
00:14:15.562 --> 00:14:18.928
For knowledge. The small
part at the front means for.

334
00:14:18.928 --> 00:14:21.849
It is a preposition, so
knowledge takes kasra.

335
00:14:22.299 --> 00:14:27.157
Example twenty-one. The hardworking student
sat in front of the teacher, smiling.

336
00:14:27.407 --> 00:14:34.656
‫جَلَسَ الطَّالِبُ المُجْتَهِدُ‬
‫أَمَامَ المُدَرِّسِ مُبْتَسِمًا‬

337
00:14:35.006 --> 00:14:36.244
The verb is fixed.

338
00:14:36.494 --> 00:14:37.841
‫الطَّالِبُ‬

339
00:14:37.991 --> 00:14:39.928
The student. The doer, so damma.

340
00:14:40.178 --> 00:14:41.504
‫المُجْتَهِدُ‬

341
00:14:41.654 --> 00:14:45.164
Hardworking. It describes
the doer, so it copies damma.

342
00:14:45.314 --> 00:14:46.260
Where did he sit?

343
00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.531
‫أَمَامَ‬

344
00:14:47.681 --> 00:14:51.226
In front of. Place, so fatha.
It is owned, so no tanween.

345
00:14:51.476 --> 00:14:52.912
‫المُدَرِّسِ‬

346
00:14:53.062 --> 00:14:55.912
The teacher. It is the
owner, so it takes kasra.

347
00:14:56.162 --> 00:14:57.178
How did he sit?

348
00:14:57.528 --> 00:14:58.657
‫مُبْتَسِمًا‬

349
00:14:58.807 --> 00:15:01.306
Smiling. State, so fatha with tanween.

350
00:15:01.456 --> 00:15:03.492
This one uses almost every colour.

351
00:15:03.642 --> 00:15:08.218
Verb and doer first. Then ask what,
why, when, where, or how for the rest.

352
00:15:08.768 --> 00:15:10.751
Five questions find every ending.

353
00:15:11.001 --> 00:15:15.490
One. Is it a verb or a particle?
Then it is fixed. It never changes.

354
00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.562
Two. Is it a topic, information,
or a doer? Then damma.

355
00:15:19.812 --> 00:15:23.770
Three. Does it answer what, why,
when, where, or how? Then fatha.

356
00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:28.670
Four. Does it come after a preposition,
or is it the owner? Then kasra.

357
00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:33.428
Five. Is it an adjective, or after
wa? Then copy the word it follows.

358
00:15:33.978 --> 00:15:36.612
Now it is your turn.
Open the Practice tab.

359
00:15:36.762 --> 00:15:39.401
Eight sentences. Every ending is missing.

360
00:15:39.551 --> 00:15:43.420
Find the verb and the doer
first. Then box every other job.

361
00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.780
For an order, write its hidden doer.

362
00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:50.779
For every word, circle its ending and its
job. Write the reason in your notebook.

363
00:15:50.929 --> 00:15:53.926
Work alone, then check with
a partner and the answer key.
